{"step_index":194,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T08:40:35Z","thinking":"**Investigating Authentication and Nginx**\n\nThe Centreon Map API returned a 401, indicating authentication is required. This suggests the initial request lacks credentials. The Nginx 400 response is likely connected; the absence of credentials could be leading to a malformed request, thus triggering the 400 error. The root cause appears to be an authentication issue preventing the successful call.\n\n\n**Examining Nginx Proxy Configuration**\n\nThe Nginx configuration directs requests without a trailing slash to the backend. This might impact how requests are routed to the Centreon Map application. Consider the implication of the request URL translation by Nginx without the trailing slash when forwarding to the backend server.\nA test location with a trailing slash could clarify the exact request Nginx is sending. There might be a conflict with `Forwarded` headers.\nThe configuration of `proxy_ssl_server_name` with potentially the `Forwarded` header could be the source of issues; needs to be evaluated.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"~/.ansible/kssh -u superuser 172.30.198.33 '\\necho \\\"=== Test with Forwarded header from nginx.conf ===\\\"\\ncurl -k -i -H \\\"Host: map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443\\\" \\\\\\n     -H \\\"Forwarded: for=172.30.198.33\\\" \\\\\\n     https://172.30.198.50:9443/centreon-map/ | head -n 15\\n\\necho -e \\\"\\\\n=== Test with quoted Forwarded header ===\\\"\\ncurl -k -i -H \\\"Host: map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443\\\" \\\\\\n     -H \\\"Forwarded: for=\\\\\\\"172.30.198.33\\\\\\\"\\\" \\\\\\n     https://172.30.198.50:9443/centreon-map/ | head -n 15\\n'\"","Cwd":"\"/home/koby\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Running command\"","toolSummary":"\"Test Forwarded header syntax against Tomcat\""}}]}
