{"step_index":206,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T08:50:12Z","thinking":"**Isolating the Nginx Configuration**\n\nThe discrepancy between the 400 and 401 status codes, based on whether the request is proxied through Nginx or made directly, needs to be understood. Adjusting the Nginx configuration, specifically on the specified server, will use a minimal `location /` configuration to proxy to the backend. The aim is to determine if any header in the `proxy.conf` file or elsewhere is causing the observed behavior.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"~/.ansible/kssh -u superuser 172.30.198.33 '\\n# Test minimal proxy configuration\\nsudo sed -i.bak_test '\\\\''/location \\\\/ {/,/}/c\\\\    location / {\\\\n        proxy_pass https://172.30.198.50:9443;\\\\n        proxy_ssl_verify off;\\\\n    }'\\\\'' /etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf\\nsudo nginx -t && sudo systemctl reload nginx\\n\\necho \\\"=== Test after minimal proxy_pass ===\\\"\\ncurl -k -i https://172.30.198.33:9443/centreon-map/ | head -n 15\\n'\"","Cwd":"\"/home/koby\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Running command\"","toolSummary":"\"Test minimal proxy_pass configuration\""}}]}
